# OrganicMarketAgent — Python Coding Standards

## Language Policy

All code, comments, docstrings, variable names, and log messages are in English.
No Hebrew in source code. See `docs/GLOSSARY.md` for canonical terminology.

---

## Stack & Versions

- Python 3.11+ only. Use `match` statements, `tomllib`, f-strings.
- SQLAlchemy 2.x — `session.execute(select(...))` style, NOT legacy `session.query()`
- httpx (async) for HTTP. No `requests` library.
- Flask for admin UI only (port 5000, 127.0.0.1).

## Project Layout

```
organic_market_agent/
  collectors/     # one file per source
  parsers/        # one parser class per normalizer_type
  normalizer/     # NormalizerEngine + DB-driven rules
  aggregator/     # AggregatorEngine, QAEngine
  publisher/      # PublishEngine, FTPSClient
  admin/          # Flask blueprints
  models/         # SQLAlchemy ORM models (one file per table group)
  db/             # session factory, Alembic env
  scheduler/      # cron wrapper, IngestionRunner
  utils/          # logging, email alert, checksum, config
  tests/          # mirrors src structure
```

## Naming & Style

- DB columns: `snake_case`
- Python functions: `snake_case`
- Classes: `PascalCase`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- Monetary values: `NUMERIC(12,4)` in DB, `Decimal` in Python — never `float`

## Error Handling

- Never silently swallow exceptions. Always log with structured context.
- Alert on: ingestion failure, publish failure, stale data threshold breach.
- Exception hierarchy: `MyFarmAgentsError > CollectorError, ParserError, PublishError`

## Data Rules

- Source of truth for product catalog, aliases, and normalizer rules = PostgreSQL (not code)
- Never hardcode product names, prices, or source URLs in logic code
- All timestamps: `TIMESTAMPTZ` in DB, `datetime` with `tzinfo=UTC` in Python
